think Opened the round with tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh, already on the anointed order, and launched the cold endurance run detached with --cadence-slice 1 before reading anything else.
think Read the card whole, then the air row of the council rota -- TAME Core, single-stranded, Gauge -- whose sense is touch: walk the fence line and press each post.
think Pressed amphora first and found a real one: vessel-core sign mints a Kumara signature over a foreign grammar, writes the file, and only then verifies, so a format amphora-v2 vessel lands carrying a stamp_sig line and then errors UnknownVersion. Reproduced on metal in a pen.
think Then read the cold run rather than only launching it, and seed_link was RED -- my own lane, the crossing, a guard already speaking while I chose a lap elsewhere.
think Bisected the crossing across this tree's own history in a detached worktree rather than reading the diff: the ratchet went 820 to 821 at 757d59171e, and its one new site is context/README.md -> ./.
think Read inseed() and found the root. It walks UP from a target looking for an allowed ancestor, which answers for a FILE. template-manifest.bron allows context/ twenty-one named pages and never the directory, so the seed makes context/ to hold them while no allow row says context.
think Patched a copy in the pen first and measured before claiming: 821 to 820, exactly one site, front-door links unmoved, no page edited and no ceiling lowered.
think Declined the second clause the same reading suggested -- a link resolving to the repository root normalises to the empty path and still reads outside -- because zero living root pages link that way, and my own last lap booked a refusal built in a field with no gate.
obs The cold run's reading was taken before any commit, and the round-open rebase that followed the claim push moved the tree under the remaining guards, so this pass closes tree_moved=yes. The two reds it named were both read and both closed here.
